IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `itaa-income`
IMPORT `itaa-income-formulas`

-- Income Tax Assessment Act 1997, ss 4-10, 61-155(2), 328-355 to 328-360, 83-170(3), 960-270, 960-275(1A) -- worked cases for
-- itaa-income-formulas.l4 (24 October 2026).
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Expected results were worked by hand from
-- the text, the Rates Act tables as restated in itaa-income.l4, and the formulas transcribed in
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/C2004A05138.formulas.md, before the encoding was run.
--
-- Jake k043 (2028-29, a sole trader riding for a food-delivery platform, $31,000): the life gives $31,000 as his income. It is
-- read here as his taxable income, his net small business income and his labour amounts alike, with no labour deductions, and
-- he is taken to be a small business entity (his turnover is far under $5 million). Those readings are the encoder's. Every
-- other figure is hypothetical, and the AWOTE figures are invented round numbers.

§ `s 61-155(2) -- net labour income`

#ASSERT `What is my net labour income` 31000 0 EQUALS 31000
#ASSERT `What is my net labour income` 60000 2500 EQUALS 57500

-- k043 with Subdivision 61-E applying: net labour income 31,000 exceeds the $18,200 threshold; the liability on it alone for
-- 2028-29 is (31,000 - 18,200) x 14% = 1,792; the offset is the lesser of $250 and that: 250.
#ASSERT `What working Australians tax offset do I get from my labour income` TRUE TRUE 2028 31000 0 EQUALS JUST 250
-- $20,000 less $3,000 of labour deductions is 17,000, not above the threshold: nil.
#ASSERT `What working Australians tax offset do I get from my labour income` TRUE TRUE 2028 20000 3000 EQUALS JUST 0
-- 2022-23 has no deposited rates: NOTHING.
#ASSERT `What working Australians tax offset do I get from my labour income` TRUE TRUE 2022 31000 0 EQUALS NOTHING

§ `ss 328-355 to 328-360 -- small business income tax offset`

-- k043: 16% x (31,000 / 31,000) x 1,792 = 286.72.
#ASSERT `What small business income tax offset do I get` 2028 TRUE FALSE 31000 31000 EQUALS `offset` 286.72
-- Half the taxable income from the business: taxable income 40,000, basic liability (40,000 - 18,200) x 14% = 3,052;
-- 16% x (20,000 / 40,000) x 3,052 = 244.16.
#ASSERT `What small business income tax offset do I get` 2028 TRUE FALSE 20000 40000 EQUALS `offset` 244.16
-- Net small business income above taxable income is cut back to it: 50,000 on 31,000 gives the same 286.72.
#ASSERT `What small business income tax offset do I get` 2028 TRUE FALSE 50000 31000 EQUALS `offset` 286.72
-- The $1,000 cap (s 328-360(2)): taxable income 200,000, all from the business, 2028-29: 26,800 x 14% = 3,752; 90,000 x 30% =
-- 27,000; 55,000 x 37% = 20,350; 10,000 x 45% = 4,500; total 55,602; 16% is 8,896.32, so $1,000.
#ASSERT `What small business income tax offset do I get` 2028 TRUE FALSE 200000 200000 EQUALS `offset` 1000
-- Not entitled under s 328-355: nil. Under 18: not covered. 2022-23: no deposited rates.
#ASSERT `What small business income tax offset do I get` 2028 FALSE FALSE 31000 31000 EQUALS `offset` 0
#ASSERT `What small business income tax offset do I get` 2028 TRUE TRUE 31000 31000 EQUALS `not covered: under 18 (s 328-375)`
#ASSERT `What small business income tax offset do I get` 2022 TRUE FALSE 31000 31000 EQUALS `not covered: no deposited rates for the year`

§ `s 4-10 -- k043's tax with the small business offset`

-- k043: 1,792 - 700 (Low Income offset) - 286.72 = 805.28 without Subdivision 61-E; 1,792 - 700 - 250 - 286.72 = 555.28 with it.
-- itaa-cases-income.l4 asserts 1,092 and 842 for k043: those leave this offset out (NOTES.md, finding 13).
#ASSERT `How much income tax do I owe with the small business offset` 2028 31000 FALSE 31000 0 TRUE FALSE 31000 EQUALS `owed` 805.28
#ASSERT `How much income tax do I owe with the small business offset` 2028 31000 TRUE 31000 0 TRUE FALSE 31000 EQUALS `owed` 555.28
-- Not a small business entity: back to itaa-income.l4's 1,092.
#ASSERT `How much income tax do I owe with the small business offset` 2028 31000 FALSE 31000 0 FALSE FALSE 31000 EQUALS `owed` 1092
-- Under 18: not covered.
#ASSERT `How much income tax do I owe with the small business offset` 2028 31000 FALSE 31000 0 TRUE TRUE 31000 EQUALS `not covered: no deposited rates for the year, or the small business offset of someone under 18`

§ `s 83-170 -- genuine redundancy`

-- 2006-07: the printed amounts, $6,783 + $3,392 x 5 years = 23,743.
#ASSERT `What is my tax-free redundancy limit` 2006 (LIST 1000) 5 EQUALS `tax-free` 23743
-- 2008-09 with November figures 1,000 (2005), 1,040 (2006), 1,040 (2007): 2007-08 factor 1.04, base 7,054.32, service 3,527.68;
-- 2008-09 factor 1.000, not indexed. 10 years: 7,054.32 + 35,276.80 = 42,331.12.
#ASSERT `What is my tax-free redundancy limit` 2008 (LIST 1000, 1040, 1040) 10 EQUALS `tax-free` 42331.12
-- A factor rounded to 3 places: 1,033.33 / 1,000 = 1.03333 -> 1.033. 2007-08, 1 year: 6,783 x 1.033 = 7,006.839 plus
-- 3,392 x 1.033 = 3,503.936: 10,510.775.
#ASSERT `What is my tax-free redundancy limit` 2007 (LIST 1000, 1033.33) 1 EQUALS `tax-free` 10510.775
-- Figures that do not reach the November before the year; a year before 2006-07: not covered.
#ASSERT `What is my tax-free redundancy limit` 2008 (LIST 1000, 1040) 10 EQUALS `not covered: the AWOTE figures do not run from November 2005 to the November before the year`
#ASSERT `What is my tax-free redundancy limit` 2005 (LIST 1000) 10 EQUALS `not covered: an income year before 2006-07`
-- A $30,000 genuine redundancy payment after 5 years in 2006-07: 23,743 tax-free. A $10,000 one: all of it. Not genuine: none.
#ASSERT `How much of my redundancy payment is tax-free` TRUE 30000 2006 (LIST 1000) 5 EQUALS `tax-free` 23743
#ASSERT `How much of my redundancy payment is tax-free` TRUE 10000 2006 (LIST 1000) 5 EQUALS `tax-free` 10000
#ASSERT `How much of my redundancy payment is tax-free` FALSE 30000 2006 (LIST 1000) 5 EQUALS `tax-free` 0
